From: alferov.s <alfaktory@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tu: free the dump_cmds list on every error path in queue_submit

queue_submit() collects the command stream entries for the read-only dump in
a local util_dynarray and frees it in the middle of the function, before the
submit is handed to the kernel. The two patchpoint resolution passes run
before that point and can append entries and then fail, taking goto out; the
list is then never released and the entries it grew stay allocated until
process exit. The paths are low frequency (only reached on an allocation
failure inside dynamic render pass resolution), but the list is per-submit
and can be large.

Free the dynarray at the out: label instead, which every exit after the
first submission attempt reaches, so it runs exactly once whether the submit
succeeds or fails.

Signed-off-by: alferov.s <alfaktory@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_queue.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_queue.cc
index 225ef8b..a68c8af 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_queue.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_queue.cc
@@ -551,8 +551,6 @@ queue_submit(struct vk_queue *_queue, struct vk_queue_submit *vk_submit)
       fd_rd_output_end(rd_output);
    }
 
-   util_dynarray_fini(&dump_cmds);
-
 #ifdef HAVE_PERFETTO
    if (u_trace_should_process(&device->trace_context)) {
       for (int i = 0; i < vk_submit->command_buffer_count; i++)
@@ -602,6 +600,7 @@ queue_submit(struct vk_queue *_queue, struct vk_queue_submit *vk_submit)
    u_trace_context_process(&device->trace_context, false);
 
 out:
+   util_dynarray_fini(&dump_cmds);
    tu_submit_finish(device, submit);
 
 fail_create_submit:
